+# Changelog
+
+## 2.0.0
+
+### Breaking changes
+
+- `nftables_base` role variables now use the `nftables_base_` prefix:
+  - `nftables_default_policy` -> `nftables_base_default_policy`
+  - `nftables_allowed_tcp_ports` -> `nftables_base_allowed_tcp_ports`
+  - `nftables_ruleset_path` -> `nftables_base_ruleset_path`
+
+### Bug fixes
+
+- `nftables_base_allowed_tcp_ports` is now actually applied to the generated
+  ruleset. Previously the variable was defined but never used, so the
+  default-drop policy silently blocked all traffic, including SSH.
+
+### Documentation
+
+- Corrected collection/role description: only Debian is declared and tested
+  (`meta/main.yml` platforms and the molecule scenario cover Debian bookworm
+  only); RedHat was never supported.
